      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, my bad. While I was about to file a bug, I found that this was already tracked as crbug.com/512509727, so I just linked that one now.\n\nThe intent here is to preserve the logical matrix value after lowering a SPIR-V `RowMajor` member to WGSL. For square matrices the WGSL type does stay as `mat4x4\u003cf32\u003e`, but `transpose(mat4x4\u003cf32\u003e)` still changes the value unless the matrix is symmetric.\n\nThe previous lowering seemed to rely on the rewritten type changing as the signal to revisit uses. That works for non-square matrices, where the physical WGSL type changes, but it misses square matrices because the physical type is unchanged. As a result, whole-matrix loads/stores and some aliases/construction/constant paths could skip the row-major conversion.\n\nI didn\u0027t benchmark my changes, so I can\u0027t tell if speed is affected.",
